# BREW Data Processing Utility - Validator Module

This module validates parsed data against defined rules.

### Validation Rules
- Field presence check
- Data type validation (integer, string, etc.)
- Range validation for numeric fields

### Functionality
- Checks each record against validation rules
- Separates valid and invalid records
- Generates validation reports

### Usage
Included in the main pipeline. Can be used standalone for validation.

### Example
```brev
import validator;

rules = {
    "id": {"type": "integer", "required": true},
    "name": {"type": "string", "required": true},
    "age": {"type": "integer", "min": 0, "max": 120, "required": true}
};

result = validator.validate(records, rules);
if result.valid {
    print("Validation passed");
} else {
    print("Validation failed:", result.errors);
}
```
